    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538-a1">

                <pb facs="0888" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg752"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 973.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blacklock to Mr. Rives.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General, United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Apia, Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 11, 1888</date>. (Received October 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 150.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Affairs in Samoa have taken a decided
                    change since last mail; then all was apparently quiet and peaceful, but now
                    everything is excitement and trouble. The whole of Samoa is in open rebellion
                    against Tamasese, and you will see from the record of current events inclosed
                    that the Tamasese Government is in a bad state.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Blacklock</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">U. S. Vice-Consul-General</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
